Alternatively, you could introduce a new trait with your desired restrictions
as a super trait:

```
# trait Foo {}
# struct Bar;
# impl Foo for Bar {}
trait Qux: Foo {} // Anything that implements Qux also needs to implement Foo
fn baz<T: Qux>(t: T) {} // also ok!
```

